From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:54:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Vampyre Slayer quest and the Blue Moon Inn bartender
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Vampyre Slayer was not implemented. Morgan always gave his
after-quest lines (the draynor script asked "completed?", which the
default assume-completed quest mode always answers with yes), and the
Blue Moon Inn had no bartender, so the quest's beer step could not be
done.

Change. New quest on the OSRS progress varp 178 (`varp.vampire`) through
the server-only varbit `vampyre_slayer_progress`: 0, 1 started, 2 stake
received, 3 complete (the cache dbrow end state, checked at startup).
These are the values Quest Helper keys its steps on. Morgan and Dr
Harlow follow the OSRS Wiki transcripts (start, legends, garlic hint,
Harlow's beer, stake, topics, a lost stake); Harlow's client varbits
`harlow_given_beer`/`harlow_given_stake` are set. Players under combat
level 20 get the transcript's warning before the start prompt, and
Morgan's first menu asks about "this vampyre" (later talks: "Count
Draynor"). Morgan's garlic cupboard opens and gives garlic. Opening the
coffin in the manor basement at stages 1-2 raises Count Draynor for that
player (removed on logout). He recovers 1 point of every stat per 5 ticks
(`regenRate = 5`, twenty times the ordinary 100). Garlic: every tick the
player has an attack queued on him (melee or autocast) while carrying
garlic, each of his stats that is full is drained: Attack -10 ("The
vampyre seems to be weakened by the garlic you're carrying." the first
time, "The vampyre seems to weaken." after), Strength -10, Defence -40
(to 0), and 10 damage (a hitsplat) when his hitpoints are full; as he
restores, the drain re-applies. Garlic also adds 1 to the player's
damage on him. At 0 hitpoints a stake and a hammer finish him (quest
complete: 3 QP, 4,825 Attack XP); otherwise he regenerates to full. If
the fight takes too long (500 ticks) he leaves, and reopening the coffin
raises him at full health. Morgan's after-quest dialogue moves from
DraynorVillageNpcs into the quest. New `BlueMoonBartender` (transcript):
"A glass of your finest ale please." sells a beer for 2 coins, plus the
fortune and equipment topics.

Tests. `VampyreSlayerInteractionTest` (12): start, decline, Harlow's
beer before the stake, a lost stake replaced, Morgan's garlic hint, the
low-combat warning, Morgan's "this vampyre" / "Count Draynor" menu, the
Count's regen rate, the garlic drain on attack, its re-application as
stats restore, no drain without garlic or an attack queued, and the +1
garlic damage. `:content:quest:test`. Manual: a full run with Quest
Helper 4.18 on the RuneLite desktop client (fresh account): every step
showed the right QH text, varp 178 went 0-1-2-3, the bartender's beer
turned QH's requirement green, and the kill completed the quest.

Data sources. Dialogue, the low-combat warning and the kill messages:
OSRS Wiki transcripts (Vampyre Slayer, Morgan, Dr Harlow, Bartender
(Blue Moon Inn)). Garlic (trigger, drains, re-application, "The vampyre
seems to weaken.", +1 damage) and stat restoration: OSRS Wiki, Count
Draynor ("Strategy", "Stat restoration"), quoting Mod Ash (Twitter 26
Jan 2020 and 17 Nov 2020; Discord 13 Aug 2025). Regeneration: Count
Draynor page ("about twenty times the rate of ordinary monsters"); the
Vampyre Slayer walkthrough says roughly 6 times, the Count Draynor value
is used. Returning to the coffin: Vampyre Slayer walkthrough note.
Rewards and locations: OSRS Wiki quest page. Step values: Quest Helper's
VampyreSlayer and the cache dbrow `quest_vampyreslayer`.

Caveats. Guesses: the cupboard's take message, "The coffin is sealed
shut." outside the quest, the Count's attack animation, the player's
coffin animation, and keeping the stake after the kill. The 500-tick
limit before he returns to his coffin is not documented and there is no
return animation (he disappears). Whether the first garlic drain prints
both messages is not documented (here only the transcript's). Zero-damage
hits stay at 0 with garlic (a miss cannot be told from a 0 roll). The
wiki's "wears off after 30 seconds" is read as the Attack restoring
(Mod Ash). The fight changes (garlic, regeneration, warning) are
unit-tested only, not yet checked in a client. Needs the quest-module patch 12 (QuestTalkFixture).

